# .templatesyncignore — files Bookkeeper OWNS, which template-sync never overwrites.
#
# Same syntax as .gitignore. The weekly template-sync workflow
# (devantler-tech/.github .github/workflows/template-sync.yaml, using
# AndreasAugustin/actions-template-sync) opens a PR that brings changes from the
# application template (the repository .github/workflows/template-sync.yaml names)
# into Bookkeeper. It only ever touches files that exist in the template, and it
# SKIPS anything matched here.
#
# Everything NOT listed here is TEMPLATE-OWNED and kept current by template-sync —
# change it upstream in the application template, never by editing it here.
# Bookkeeper receives .github/workflows/{release,template-sync,stale-issues,codeql}.yaml,
# .coderabbit.yaml, zizmor.yml and CLAUDE.md. It owns the rest of what the template
# ships: its CI and CD, its lint configuration, its code and the template's tenant
# plumbing, which a Bookkeeper that is not a publish-app tenant does not use.
#
# merge-template-ignore-entries is on, so each sync ADDS the template's entries this
# list lacks: a file the template later marks as application-owned stays Bookkeeper's.
# To receive a file the template lists, add the line `!<entry>` here instead.

# --- Identity & docs (Bookkeeper's own) ---
AGENTS.md
README.md
CONTRIBUTING.md
LICENSE
.github/CODEOWNERS
.claude/skills/maintain/SKILL.md
# docs/ is Bookkeeper's own. The template's docs/REFERENCE.md describes the template's
# scaffold and tenant publishing, which Bookkeeper does not use, and its long table rows
# exceed the 400-character line limit of Bookkeeper's Markdown lint.
docs/

# --- CI, release and dependency config Bookkeeper tailors ---
# ci.yaml calls the shared Go validator. Bookkeeper's cd.yaml releases its binaries with
# GoReleaser and publish.yaml publishes its signed image and chart; the template's cd.yaml
# is the platform-tenant publish path instead.
.github/workflows/ci.yaml
.github/workflows/cd.yaml
.github/workflows/publish.yaml
.github/workflows/todos.yaml
# The template's Dependabot file is .yml; Bookkeeper's is .yaml.
.github/dependabot.yml
.github/dependabot.yaml
.releaserc
.goreleaser.yaml
.ko.yaml
.gitignore
# .golangci.yml is Bookkeeper's on purpose: its depguard rule is a strict allowlist,
# which Bookkeeper extends with its own dependencies.
.golangci.yml
cspell.json
Dockerfile
# No GitHub Copilot features in this repository; never restore the agent setup workflow.
.github/workflows/copilot-setup-steps.yml

# --- Lint configuration ---
# Bookkeeper's .mega-linter.yml stands alone: it excludes the Helm chart templates from
# the YAML linters and does not extend the template's shared base, and the shared Go
# validator runs MegaLinter, not the template's lint workflow. Without its own yamllint
# or markdownlint file, MegaLinter's bundled rules apply. Receiving the template's copies
# would change what lint enforces on every file; adopting the shared base is a change of
# its own.
.mega-linter.yml
.github/mega-linter.base.yml
.github/workflows/lint.yaml
.yamllint.yml
.markdownlint.json

# --- The application's overlays on shared configuration ---
.github/codeql/codeql-config.yml

# --- Platform-tenant plumbing (Bookkeeper does not publish through publish-app) ---
# The same files the template's scaffold removes and lists without --tenancy, and the
# fixture their tests read. Remove these lines, and copy the files from the template, to
# become a tenant.
deploy/
renovate.json
scripts/publish-pin-approved.sh
scripts/publish-pin-approved.test.sh
scripts/workflow-caller-pin-contract.test.sh
scripts/fixtures/own-publisher.yaml
# The queue check the template's own ci.yaml runs against its tenant cd.yaml publication queue.
scripts/validate-workflow-queues.sh

# --- Bookkeeper's own application ---
# Ignored wholesale, so a template file added later at a path Bookkeeper already uses
# can never touch its code.
go.mod
go.sum
main.go
cmd/
internal/
pkg/
charts/

